@Controller("/shoppingMall/products/:productId/images")
export class ShoppingmallProductsImagesController {
  /**
   * Reorder the display sequence of images for a specific product. This operation allows sellers to control which image appears as the main thumbnail by rearranging the image gallery order.
   *
   * The first image in the new order becomes the main thumbnail displayed in product listings and search results. All active (non-deleted) images must be included in the reorder request - partial updates are not supported. The display_order field is updated for each image based on its position in the provided array.
   *
   * This endpoint is restricted to sellers who own the product. When the image order is updated, a product snapshot is automatically created to preserve the previous image state for historical order references and dispute resolution. This ensures that order items can reference the exact product appearance at the time of purchase.
   *
   * Soft-deleted images (those with deleted_at set) are excluded from the reorder operation and should not be included in the request. Only active images should be provided in the reorder array.
   *
   * Related operations: POST /sellers/products/{productId}/images for uploading new images, DELETE /sellers/products/{productId}/images/{imageId} for removing individual images, GET /products/{productId} for viewing the product with its current image order.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param productId Target product's ID (UUID format). The product must be owned by the requesting seller.
   * @param body Ordered array of image IDs defining the new display sequence. First element becomes the main thumbnail. Must include all active image IDs for the product.
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor null
   * @x-autobe-specification Update the display order of product images for a specific product. Validate that the requesting user is a seller and owns the product. Verify all provided image IDs belong to the specified product and no images are missing or duplicated. Update the display_order field for each image based on their position in the provided array (first element gets display_order 1, second gets 2, etc.). Create a product snapshot before updating to preserve the previous state for historical order references. Return the updated list of images with their new display order. Handle soft-deleted images by excluding them from the reorder operation. If any validation fails (product not found, seller doesn't own product, image IDs don't match product, duplicate or missing images), return appropriate error response.
