@Controller("/shoppingMall/customer/reviews/:reviewId/snapshots")
export class ShoppingmallCustomerReviewsSnapshotsController {
  /**
   * Retrieve a paginated list of historical snapshots for a specific review.
   *
   * This endpoint provides access to the complete audit trail of review modifications, showing the state of the review at each point in time when it was edited or deleted. Each snapshot captures the rating and content as they existed before the change was applied.
   *
   * **Authorization**: Only sellers and administrators can access review snapshots. Sellers can view snapshots for reviews on products they sell. Administrators can view snapshots for any review on the platform. Customers cannot access review snapshots, even for their own reviews.
   *
   * **Use Cases**: This operation supports dispute resolution by providing evidence of what a review contained at any historical point. It enables verification of review modifications and maintains transparency in the review system.
   *
   * **Related Operations**: Use GET /products/{productId}/reviews to view current active reviews for a product. Use PUT /customers/reviews/{reviewId} to edit a review, which automatically creates a new snapshot.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param reviewId Target review's ID to retrieve snapshots for
   * @param body Search criteria and pagination parameters for review snapshots
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor customer
   * @x-autobe-specification Query shopping_mall_review_snapshots table filtered by shopping_mall_review_id matching the reviewId path parameter.
   *
   * Apply authorization checks: verify requesting user is seller or admin. For sellers, validate they own products that have reviews matching this reviewId by joining through shopping_mall_reviews to shopping_mall_products.
   *
   * Support pagination with page and limit query parameters. Default limit to 20 items per page. Sort results by snapshot_at descending (newest snapshots first) to show most recent changes first.
   *
   * Return snapshot summary including id, rating, content (nullable), snapshot_at timestamp, and snapshot_by_user_id. Include pagination metadata with total count, current page, and page size.
   *
